  "review_decisions": [
    "Hölder is generalized in place to arbitrary measure spaces and both endpoint cases.",
    "Young convolution retains the general group theorem, adds the Euclidean convention through the existing convolution entry, and corrects the unjustified endpoint density/unique-extension argument.",
    "The product of complete Lebesgue measures requires completion to recover the full Lebesgue sigma-algebra.",
    "Sigma-finiteness, real powers, extended infima and complex moduli are explicit newly exposed dependencies.",
    "Mixed measurable norms are distinguished from Bochner spaces when the spatial exponent is infinity.",
    "Parabolic measure nullity is not interpreted as absence of singular points; PDE partial regularity belongs to B14.",
    "The displayed difference, interpolation, uniform-limit, and differentiation arguments are direct derivations under the stated hypotheses.",
    "The reused product-measure definition exposed a distinct product-sigma-algebra prerequisite; it is now separated and grounded through generated sigma-algebras.",
    "Nonnegative extended sums and the zero-times-infinity integration convention are made explicit at the measure foundation.",
    "Measure completeness is separated from metric completeness; completion, Hausdorff dimension and strong measurability have dedicated definitions.",
    "The two pre-existing topology-index label findings and the existing Holder-to-metric-uniform-continuity label finding are retained after semantic inspection; their target meanings are appropriate."
  ],
